INT. SALT MINE - ELEVATOR CAGE - NIGHT

Two hundred meters down. White walls. Dripping brine.

Four figures in grey coveralls crowd the cage. Hard hats. Headlamps.

RAFFERTY "RAFF" OYELARAN-STEIN. Late 40s. Planner. Calm hands.

MIRELA "MOUSE" DRAGOMIR. 20s. Safecracker. Chews her lip.

TOBIAS VANTERPOOL. 60s. Retired mine foreman. Knows every shaft.

KENJI "KITE" NAKAGAWA-REYES. 30s. Driver. Jittery.

The cage shudders. Stops.

KITE
We stopped.

TOBIAS
We're there.

RAFF
Lamps off. On my count.

They click off. Black. A drip. A breath.

RAFF (CONT'D)
Mouse. Where's the vault?

MOUSE
Four hundred meters east. Behind a wall of rock salt.

RAFF
Tobias?

TOBIAS
Old drift. Sealed in sixty-four. I know the way, Raff.

RAFF
Kite, you stay with the cage.

KITE
Why do I always stay with the cage?

RAFF
Because the cage is how we leave.

Lamps on. They step out. Salt crunches underfoot.

INT. SALT MINE - MAIN DRIFT - CONTINUOUS

A tunnel. Rails. An abandoned ore cart.

Tobias leads. Mouse behind. Raff last. Their lamps carve white cones in the dark.

MOUSE
Tobias, how deep is the vault wall?

TOBIAS
Two meters. Salt. Soft, but it carries sound.

MOUSE
Then no drill.

TOBIAS
No drill.

Raff stops. Holds up a fist. The other two freeze.

A distant HUM. A headlight sweeps across the far end of the tunnel. An automatic ore train, no driver.

RAFF
(whisper)
Ore train. Down.

All three drop behind the ore cart. Lamps off. Tobias presses a hand over Mouse's shoulder. She flinches, then steadies.

The train grinds past. Its headlight slides over the cart. Stops.

TOBIAS
(barely audible)
Don't breathe.

The beam holds, searching. Mouse's eyes are huge. Raff's hand eases toward a rubber mallet at his belt.

A relay CLACKS. The track switches.

The beam swings away. The train recedes. The three exhale together.

MOUSE
That was...

RAFF
Still on schedule. Move.

They rise. They move faster.

INT. SALT MINE - SEALED DRIFT - LATER

A wall of grey-white salt. A rusted door half buried in it.

Tobias taps the wall. Listens.

TOBIAS
Here.

MOUSE
Raff, I need ten minutes.

RAFF
You have six.

MOUSE
Raff.

RAFF
Mouse. Six.

She kneels. Unrolls a canvas kit. Brushes, a stethoscope, a tiny hammer.

Tobias takes a position at the corner. Raff paces.

RAFF (CONT'D)
(into radio, low)
Kite. Status.

KITE (V.O.)
(radio)
Cage is fine. I'm fine. Everyone's fine. Why do you ask?

RAFF
Stay on the line.

KITE (V.O.)
(radio)
Raff, there's a light coming down the main shaft.

Raff stops pacing. Tobias turns.

RAFF
How far?

KITE (V.O.)
(radio)
Forty meters, maybe. The second cage is dropping.

TOBIAS
Haul run. It's early.

RAFF
Mouse!

MOUSE
Four minutes!

RAFF
You have two!

Mouse bites down on the stethoscope. Turns a dial by feel. Click. Click. Click-CLUNK.

The door sags inward. Behind it: a steel cabinet, a stack of velvet cases.

MOUSE
Open!

Tobias and Raff haul the door wide. Mouse scoops cases into a duffel. Tobias checks the corridor.

TOBIAS
Raff! Alarm!

An alarm BLARES down the drift. Strobes pulse white on the salt.

RAFF
(grabbing the duffel)
Run!

They scatter down the drift, lamps swinging wildly, salt dust boiling up behind them.

INT. SALT MINE - ELEVATOR CAGE - CONTINUOUS

Kite hears the pounding feet before he sees them. Raff, Mouse, Tobias burst out of the dark.

KITE
Go go go go!

They pile in. Kite slams the lever. The cage lurches upward.

Below, the strobes flicker between the bars. Then the dark swallows them.

The cage rattles up through the rock. Four chests heaving. No one speaks.

Finally Mouse laughs. A short, breathless bark.

MOUSE
Six minutes.

RAFF
(grinning despite himself)
Five.

KITE
I stayed with the cage.

TOBIAS
You did.

The cage keeps climbing toward a thin line of stars.
